#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:2
msgid "Cloud Dedicated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:4
msgid ""
"Mattermost Cloud Dedicated is designed for larger organizations with "
"higher demands for performance, scalability, customizability, and "
"compliance looking to offload operational overhead and focus on more "
"business-critical tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:6
msgid ""
"Your own private Mattermost instance running :doc:`Mattermost Enterprise "
"</product-overview/editions-and-offerings>` is a Kubernetes cluster "
"hosted and managed by Mattermost that runs on dedicated cloud "
"infrastructure, where resources are exclusively available for your "
"organization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:9
msgid "Reference architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:11
msgid ""
"An architecture diagram showing the components of the Mattermost Cloud "
"Dedicated solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:15
msgid "Available features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:18
msgid "Zero-downtime upgrades"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:20
msgid ""
"Mattermost releases biweekly updates and leverages recurring maintenance "
"windows to keep your instance up-to-date with new stable or beta features"
" behind feature flags, fix security issues, and ensure the overall "
"reliability and performance of your environment. Maintenance windows are "
"announced in advance on https://status.mattermost.com/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:22
msgid ""
"Additional support options, including quicker response times, dedicated "
"support personnel, and stronger service level agreements (SLAs), are also"
" available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:25
msgid "Disaster Recovery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:27
msgid ""
"Mattermost Cloud Dedicated supports data failover to a secondary "
"region/site should the primary instance experiences an unrecoverable "
"outage with guaranteed recovery times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:29
msgid ""
"Mattermost supports a **multi-AZ (availability zones)** strategy in the "
"same site/region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:31
msgid ""
"Daily backups of the database, object storage, and high availability "
"clusters are captured and retained for 30 days."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:33
msgid ""
"In addition, highly available observability tools with automated "
"alerting, long-term metrics, and logs retention are retained for a "
"duration of 1 year, or longer, if requred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:36
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:38
msgid ""
"You have access to all the resources required to run the Mattermost "
"application with the highest security standards, including data "
"encryption at rest and in transit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:40
msgid ""
"Your pre-configured cluster is secure by default, based on industry best "
"practices including Data encryption at rest and in transit, TLS "
"certificates life cycle management, and automatic security updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:42
msgid ""
"Mattermost maintains control over network and security policies, "
"including `encryption <#encryption>`__, database, data, object storage, "
"backup schedules, and compliance certifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:45
msgid "Authentication and authorization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:47
msgid ""
"Mattermost offers advanced security and authentication options for "
"integrating with corporate directories, including :doc:`Active "
"Directory/LDAP </administration-guide/onboard/ad-ldap>`, :doc:`Okta "
"</administration-guide/onboard/sso-saml-okta>`, :doc:`OneLogin "
"</administration-guide/onboard/sso-saml-onelogin>`, :doc:`SAML "
"</administration-guide/onboard/sso-saml>`, :doc:`Google </administration-"
"guide/onboard/sso-google>`, :doc:`EntraID </administration-guide/onboard"
"/sso-entraid>`, and :doc:`OpenID </administration-guide/onboard/sso-"
"openidconnect>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:50
msgid "Secure networking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:52
msgid ""
"Mattermost Cloud Dedicated supports :doc:`IP filtering </administration-"
"guide/manage/cloud-ip-filtering>` through CIDR-based IP ranges, providing"
" flexibility for system administrators to include various authorized IPs "
"or IP ranges for seamless access control. Users attempting to access "
"their :doc:`workspace </end-user-guide/end-user-guide-index>` from IPs "
"outside defined ranges are restricted from entry. Cloud system admins can"
" :ref:`configure IP filtering <administration-guide/manage/cloud-ip-"
"filtering:configure ip filtering>` through their Mattermost System "
"Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:55
msgid "Encryption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:57
msgid ""
"Mattermost provides encryption-in-transit and encryption-at-rest "
"capabilities. Mattermost supports :doc:`TLS encryption </deployment-"
"guide/server/setup-tls>`, including AES-256 with 2048-bit RSA on all data"
" transmissions, between Mattermost client applications and the Mattermost"
" server. You may either set up TLS on the Mattermost Server or "
":doc:`install a proxy such as NGINX </deployment-guide/server/setup-"
"nginx-proxy>`, and set up TLS on the proxy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:59
msgid ""
"Connections to :doc:`Active Directory/LDAP </administration-guide/onboard"
"/ad-ldap>` can :ref:`optionally be secured with TLS or stunnel "
"<administration-guide/configure/authentication-configuration-"
"settings:ad/ldap port>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:61
msgid "Connections to calls are secured with a combination of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:63
msgid "TLS: The existing WebSocket channel is used to secure the signaling path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:64
msgid ""
"DTLS v1.2 (mandatory): Used for initial key exchange. Supports "
"``TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256`` and "
"``TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA`` algorithms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:65
msgid ""
"SRTP (mandatory): Used to encrypt all media packets (i.e. those "
"containing voice or screen share). Supports ``AEAD_AES_128_GCM`` and "
"``AES128_CM_HMAC_SHA1_80`` algorithms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:68
msgid "Cloud native exports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/cloud-dedicated.rst:70
msgid ""
"Mattermost supports optional :ref:`filestore configuration settings "
"<administration-guide/configure/environment-configuration-settings:enable"
" dedicated export filestore target>` to direct compliance and bulk export"
" data to a separate S3 bucket from standard files. This separate bucket "
"can be configured to allow for secure access by Mattermost Cloud teams as"
" well as admins who manage a given Mattermost deployment. The exports can"
" also be accessed by generating unique download links as needed."
msgstr ""

